
               #################################################
               Equilibrated AMOEBA Water Boxes for MD Simulation
               #################################################

      This directory contains a several water boxes that are equilibrated
      using the AMOEBA 2003 water model. The "water03.prm" file contains
      the parameters used for the MD equilibration of each box. The boxes
      are cubes of size ranging from 30 Ang on a side to 120 Ang in 5 Ang
      increments. For example, "water80.xyz" and "water80.key" correspond
      to an 80 Ang cubic system.

      As per the "water03.prm" parameter file, the atom types are 1 for
      the oxygen atom and 2 for the hydrogens. These atom type numbers can
      be changed as needed using the Tinker XYZEDIT program. For example,
      the water atom types in the "amoebabio18.prm" parameters are 349 for
      the oxygen and 350 for the hydrogens instead of 1 and 2.

      The equilibration of these boxes is specific the AMOEBA 2003 water
      model. Use of other AMOEBA-like models should only require minimal
      MD equilibration with the different model. For use with TIP3P or
      other nonpolarizable models, the box should first be reminimized
      and then reequilibrated via MD simulation.

